infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What each tool dispatches: fireEvent vs user-event
  desc fireEvent teleports one synthetic event; user-event replays the real device sequence under browser constraints
  compares
    - label fireEvent — one synthetic event
      children
        - label click fires 1 MouseEvent
          desc A lone synthetic click that lands on disabled, unfocusable, or covered nodes.
        - label change teleports 1 value
          desc Sets the value wholesale, ignoring maxLength, readonly, and every keydown handler.
        - label No focus, no device state
          desc Skips the pointer and focus side effects a real interaction produces.
        - label Greenlights impossible states
          desc Asserts input states a user could never produce through the UI.
    - label user-event v14 — the real sequence
      children
        - label click fires about 9 events
          desc pointerover to down to focus to up to click, in order, with focus side effects.
        - label type fires 4 events per key (80+ for 20 chars)
          desc keydown, keypress, input, keyup per character, honoring maxLength and selection.
        - label Async so React can flush
          desc Every API awaits between events; a missing await races assertions into act warnings.
        - label Refuses impossible interactions
          desc Throws on pointer-events none — when user.click throws, a real user is blocked too.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
